WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.560
Black Panther director Ryan Coogler&nbsp;
will be developing a new series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:10.240
set in Wakanda on Disney+. Here are some&nbsp;
stories Black Panther fans want to see in it.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.240
Vibranium is the miraculous metal with&nbsp;
sound-absorbing properties that is the basis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.320
of both Wakanda's enormous wealth&nbsp;
and its technological wizardry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:25.600
It's one of the most powerful substances on&nbsp;
the planet. Almost all of it is in Wakanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.320
and what little exists outside of it has&nbsp;
already been enough to change the world.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.680
"Cap's shield is made out of Vibranium.&nbsp;
They made Vision's body out of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.200
Black Panther's suit is made out of it."

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.800
The bulk of it crashed down to Earth in the form&nbsp;
of a meteorite ages ago. The local warriors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.200
led by a man named Bashenga, fearlessly&nbsp;
visited the site and discovered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.760
material's unique properties and&nbsp;
set about using it to make weapons.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.640
However, the strong radiation from the&nbsp;
Vibranium mutated some of the tribesmen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:04.560
into "Demon Spirits." Bashenga drew strength&nbsp;
from the Panther God and defeated these menaces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.680
and his strength and leadership united&nbsp;
all of the tribes and formed Wakanda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.960
Bashenga became the Black Panther, creating&nbsp;
a dynasty that would last through the ages.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.880
Considering that all of the Black&nbsp;
Panther ancestors are accessible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.720
through the trance-like communion&nbsp;
in the Heart-Shaped Herb ceremony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.880
there's an easy way to bring this&nbsp;
narrative into the modern day. Bashenga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.880
the discovery of Vibranium, and the founding&nbsp;
of Wakanda could be its own extended story arc.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.240
“It was built on a mound of the most&nbsp;
valuable metal known to man. 'Isipho,'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:41.120
they call it. The gift. Vibranium."

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.760
There is also an opportunity to&nbsp;
introduce a number of new characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.760
expand on the origins of each of the tribes.&nbsp;
If Vibranium itself is the focus of the arc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:57.280
the story of how the Great Mound was sealed off,&nbsp;
protected, and mined over the years and how that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:03.120
affected local politics and culture has a lot&nbsp;
of possibilities as well. The decision to hide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.240
Wakanda's advanced nature from the rest of the&nbsp;
world is another potential story of its own.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.400
"This never gets old."

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:15.520
M'Baku was one of the breakout&nbsp;
characters of the Black Panther movie.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.760
The chieftain of the Jabari Tribe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.600
he challenges T'Challa for the kingship&nbsp;
of Wakanda in ritual combat and loses.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:27.440
Living in the mountains, the Jabari&nbsp;
separated themselves from the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.960
tribes and were generally hostile.&nbsp;
However, M'Baku comes to T'Challa's aid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.760
when Killmonger steals the throne and even&nbsp;
becomes a huge part of Wakanda's defense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.080
when Thanos invades Earth. He also&nbsp;
has a pretty good sense of humor.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.440
"One more word, and I will&nbsp;
feed you to my children."

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.160
"I am kidding, we are vegetarians."

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.320
In the comics, he is a much more sinister figure,&nbsp;
as he directly tries to usurp the throne and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.320
betrays T'Challa's friendship. Then&nbsp;
he becomes a full-on supervillain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.040
taking on the power of the sacred White&nbsp;
Gorilla. However, he always keeps his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:11.760
Jabari tribesmen in mind and protects them even&nbsp;
while he rejects the modernization of Wakanda.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.240
"Witness the might of the Jabari, firsthand!"

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.640
One element from the comics that&nbsp;
could be fruitful for M'Baku's story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.320
is the introduction of his&nbsp;
cousin, Chante Giovanni Brown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:32.080
a Jabari native who grew up in America. She dubbs&nbsp;
herself "Queen Divine Justice" and grows up as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:38.000
normal American teenager until she is summoned&nbsp;
home to become one of the new Dora Milaje.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.280
This could all fit into M'Baku's story&nbsp;
after the events of Avengers: Infinity War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.480
Did he have a hand in ruling Wakanda in&nbsp;
T'Challa's absence? What role did the Jabari&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:54.240
have in the post-Thanos world? Fleshing out&nbsp;
the Jabari society and history as they adjust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:58.560
to becoming a more active part of Wakanda&nbsp;
could be an entire story arc of its own.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.520
T'Challa's father T'Chaka was the last Wakandan&nbsp;
king to hide how advanced the nation was from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.320
the rest of the world. As advanced as&nbsp;
his anti-surveillance technology was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.360
even he had difficulty keeping out all invaders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:18.480
especially when betrayed by one of his&nbsp;
own. T'Chaka established a worldwide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.800
network of Wakandan spies and operatives&nbsp;
and sent his brother N'Jobu to America.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:31.840
Seeing racial injustice in America and beyond,&nbsp;
N'Jobu rejected Wakanda's noninterference policies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:37.840
and worked with the mercenary Ulysses Klaue&nbsp;
to steal Vibranium. N'Jobu compromised the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:44.160
existence of Wakanda in order to get what he&nbsp;
wanted, forcing T'Chaka's hand as he killed him.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:51.280
T'Chaka leaving behind N'Jobu's son N'Jadaka,&nbsp;
aka Erik Killmonger, to be raised as an orphan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:56.560
was a questionable moral decision. This raises&nbsp;
the question: What other tough decisions did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:02.240
T'Chaka make during his reign? How did he&nbsp;
shape the Wakanda that T'Challa inherited?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.040
"I am sure you did what is right for Wakanda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:12.080
You always do. You are a great king, Baba.&nbsp;
And that is why you will always reign."]

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:16.320
T'Chaka demonstrated that he was willing&nbsp;
to kill a member of his own family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.320
in order to protect his country,&nbsp;
so who else did he have to kill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:26.160
especially as superheroes and villains started&nbsp;
appearing? How aware was T'Chaka of beings like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:31.920
the Eternals? How much did he teach T'Challa as he&nbsp;
was growing up, and how much did he keep hidden?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.800
What was his relationship with his wife, Queen&nbsp;
Ramonda , like? There could be a great deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.840
of backstory established for modern-day&nbsp;
Wakanda as T'Chaka's life is explored.

00:05:43.274 --> 00:05:51.840
Nakia was introduced in Black Panther as a&nbsp;
spy and T'Challa's on-again, off-again lover.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:53.460
"Hi."

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.200
This was a sharp break from the comics,&nbsp;
where Nakia was one of two Dora Milaje,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:04.800
but her obsession with T'Challa eventually&nbsp;
warped into her becoming the deadly assassin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:08.880
Malice. The Nakia of the MCU is a far nobler soul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.480
but they barely scratched the surface&nbsp;
of her character in the movie.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.640
A story arc following Nakia's career&nbsp;
undercover would be fascinating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:21.440
starting with what led her to choose a career&nbsp;
that took her outside Wakanda so often.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.040
Her desire to make a difference&nbsp;
in other countries by infiltrating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.680
and destroying human trafficking rings,&nbsp;
for example, revealed her overall goals.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.320
"I can't be happy knowing that there's&nbsp;
people out there who have nothing."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.680
What other kinds of missions did she carry&nbsp;
out? The idea that she was especially keen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:44.320
on protecting women and children worldwide is&nbsp;
a fascinating one because of her willingness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:50.480
to put herself into compromising situations.&nbsp;
Another question to answer would be how and if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:55.200
she had to make tough ethical decisions with&nbsp;
regard to perhaps pretending to be part of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.920
corrupt organization or assassinating its&nbsp;
leaders. Only the vaguest details of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.440
career have been revealed, and this could have&nbsp;
direct relevance to her current life in the MCU.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:10.720
Revealing what happened to Nakia after Thanos&nbsp;
disappeared T'Challa and half of creation for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:15.760
five years would make for a fascinating story&nbsp;
arc. Is she still advancing humanitarian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:20.640
interests as part of a new Wakanda? Or have&nbsp;
hard times made her an ever harder person?

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.760
The story of the lovers Ayo and&nbsp;
Aneka was explored in detail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:30.640
in the World of Wakanda series, and it&nbsp;
could easily be adapted for television.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:36.320
Both were members of the Dora Milaje who found&nbsp;
themselves rebelling against the monarchy.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:41.200
Aneka killed a village chief who was abusing&nbsp;
women, but killing him was still forbidden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:46.400
Aneka was sentenced to death. Ayo pleaded&nbsp;
to Queen Ramonda on Aneka's behalf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:52.080
and while Ramonda was sympathetic, she chose to&nbsp;
follow the law to its letter. Ayo freed Aneka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.880
and they stole high-tech Midnight Angels armor.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:59.920
Fleeing the city, they helped Jabari&nbsp;
tribeswomen and started routing bandits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:05.600
who were abusing women. Taking in these women,&nbsp;
they became their own self-styled Dora Milaje.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.360
They made an alliance with the&nbsp;
Jabari and another breakaway group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:14.560
the People, even though their motives&nbsp;
seemed questionable. At the urging of Shuri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:19.200
they helped defeat the People's attempt&nbsp;
at overthrowing T'Challa. In response,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:25.120
T'Challa declared Wakanda to be a democracy,&nbsp;
remaining king but only in a representative role.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:29.920
In the wake of the power vacuum of T'Challa&nbsp;
being snapped from existence in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:34.640
this is a story that could be adapted even&nbsp;
more readily. A Wakanda without the strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.040
influence of T'Challa is one that could&nbsp;
lapse into abuse. Seeing a story where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.480
justice and freedom butt up against regimented&nbsp;
traditions is one that would be deeply resonant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:49.840
and the love story between Ayo and Aneka&nbsp;
would add another dimension to Wakandan lore.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.040
In the comics, the Hatut Zeraze,&nbsp;
also known as the "Dogs of War",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.200
were the Wakandan secret police.&nbsp;
King T'Chaka used them extensively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:03.680
to repel invaders and assassinate&nbsp;
political enemies across the globe.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.480
They were led by Hunter, the "White Wolf,"&nbsp;
who wore armor similar to T'Challa's,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:14.400
only all in white. The Hatut Zeraze wore&nbsp;
similar armor and carried heavy ordnance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.840
as soldiers and assassins. Hunter was&nbsp;
T'Challa's adopted brother. King T'Chaka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.720
found him as an infant after he was in a&nbsp;
plane crash and raised him as his own son.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:28.960
Being Caucasian, Hunter wasn't fully&nbsp;
accepted by many other Wakandans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:35.040
and he grew up jealous of T'Challa. The Black&nbsp;
Panther exiled Hunter and the Hatut Zeraze when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:40.960
he became king because he had no interest in using&nbsp;
an assassination squad. Hunter later went on to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:46.560
on separate occasions, both provide aid&nbsp;
to T'Challa, and attempt to kill him.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:51.440
None of these characters have been introduced in&nbsp;
the MCU, but it's not much of a leap to introduce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:56.720
them, given the movie T'Chaka's demonstrated&nbsp;
willingness to kill enemies of the state. Given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:01.920
a destabilized Wakanda, introducing Hunter&nbsp;
and bringing him out of exile in an effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:07.200
to seize power and "bring order" could make&nbsp;
him a powerful villain in the Wakanda series.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:11.920
Like all of the best villains, he sees&nbsp;
himself as a hero. Like his adopted father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:16.600
he sees himself as being someone who can&nbsp;
make hard decisions when no one else can.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:21.840
One of the greatest villains of Christopher&nbsp;
Priest's run on Black Panther was the Reverend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:28.640
Doctor Michael Ibn al-Hajj Achebe . A native&nbsp;
of Wakandan neighbor Ghudaza , he was a simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:34.400
farmer until rebels from another country came. He&nbsp;
nursed them back to health, but his wife fell in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.920
love with their leader. They left Achebe for dead&nbsp;
and thirsting for vengeance. He made a deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:46.960
the devil Mephisto , took bloody vengeance, and&nbsp;
then went to America and got an education at Yale.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:53.280
Achebe had his eye on Wakanda and its resources&nbsp;
and manipulated politics to stoke a civil war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:58.800
that forced refugees into Wakanda. He&nbsp;
manipulated T'Challa into going to America&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:04.240
and tried to take the crown, but T'Challa&nbsp;
severed Achebe's relationship with Mephisto and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:09.760
beat him. Of course, Achebe became even more&nbsp;
unhinged, designing demented death traps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:15.520
for the Panther and talking to a hand puppet&nbsp;
named Daki . Achebe's twisted sense of humor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:21.600
and grandiose personality make him a perfect&nbsp;
foil to the cool, calculating Black Panther.

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:28.320
Like Hunter and the Hatut Zeraze, Achebe could&nbsp;
be a perfect villain in a destabilized Wakanda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:34.000
Without having to deal with T'Challa, he could&nbsp;
easily try to become a demented populist leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:39.520
a twisted advisor to whoever's in power, a&nbsp;
cult leader, or any number of other roles.

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:46.000
The Panther Cult and the White Gorilla Cult&nbsp;
aren't the only religions in Wakanda. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.880
many of the tribes worshipped their own gods.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:54.000
Sekhmet , the Lion God, was originally an&nbsp;
Egyptian deity who tried to establish a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:59.360
presence in Wakanda. Unlike the Panther&nbsp;
God, who only appeared to his priests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:05.440
the Lion God freely appeared before humans.&nbsp;
However, her violent nature didn't exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:10.560
make her a popular candidate for worship.&nbsp;
She even attacked T'Challa directly in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.400
attempt to gain the Panther God's&nbsp;
secrets, but she was defeated.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:18.000
The Panther Cult was created&nbsp;
by the Egyptian goddess Bast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:23.360
Other gods, such as Sobek the Crocodile&nbsp;
God, also had their followers in Wakanda.

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:29.520
This history of clashing gods could all inspire&nbsp;
a mystical and magical arc on the Wakanda show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:35.840
as various sects new and old challenge the&nbsp;
Panther Cult for control of the soul of Wakanda.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:40.080
Even if it's in the background, the show&nbsp;
should certainly explore the many religions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.520
represented in this rich and&nbsp;
expansive fictional world.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:50.800
In the comics, Wakanda and Atlantis went from&nbsp;
having a tense coexistence to outright war. King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:55.840
T'Chaka allied himself briefly with Prince Namor&nbsp;
the Sub-Mariner in a battle against the Nazis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.840 --> 00:13:00.240
although he still kept Wakanda a&nbsp;
secret from the rest of the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:05.680
T'Chaka knew Namor was a loose cannon and kept an&nbsp;
eye on him. When T'Challa became king, he nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:12.160
got into a war with Atlantis over a territory&nbsp;
that both claimed, but cooler heads prevailed.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.520
Later, in a conflict between&nbsp;
the Avengers and X-Men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:20.080
Namor turned against his old teammates&nbsp;
and tracked them to Wakanda. He used his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:26.160
temporary Phoenix-force powers to wipe out much of&nbsp;
Wakanda. Later, when Shuri was queen of Wakanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:31.920
she retaliated by destroying Atlantis. Namor&nbsp;
got revenge by setting Thanos on Wakanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:37.520
telling him that the Wakandans held an&nbsp;
Infinity Stone. Things simply went too far.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:42.800
Namor and Atlantis have yet to be introduced&nbsp;
in the MCU. The Black Panther franchise would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:47.840
be a great launching point. There's even what&nbsp;
one might consider an allusion to Atlantis in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:53.520
Avengers: Endgame, when Okoye refers to&nbsp;
an underwater earthquake near Wakanda.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.000
"Do we have a visual? How&nbsp;
are we handling it?" "Nat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.800 --> 00:14:01.840
It's an earthquake under the ocean.&nbsp;
We handle it by not handling it."

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.520
Namor would make a powerful anti-hero in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:10.480
being a generally noble figure who has good&nbsp;
reason to be angry at the surface world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:15.840
easily turning from antagonist to hero&nbsp;
over the course of a single storyline.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:21.680
T'Challa's mother Queen Ramonda was a somewhat&nbsp;
underserved character in Black Panther.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:25.440
She was there to see her son named as&nbsp;
king and then traveled to the land of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.080
the Jabari in an effort to heal him. The&nbsp;
Wakanda series could go into much greater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:35.200
depth regarding her character. How tuned in&nbsp;
was she regarding the activities of her husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:40.560
T'Chaka? Did she approve of him killing his&nbsp;
brother in order to preserve Wakandan secrets?

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:46.000
More interesting than that is what Ramonda did&nbsp;
when both T'Challa and Shuri disappeared for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:52.160
five years. Okoye took her place as one of the&nbsp;
Avengers, but what role did Ramonda play in this?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:57.360
Was she the default monarch of Wakanda? Did&nbsp;
she have to fend off attempts at the crown?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:01.040
Seeing her having to deal&nbsp;
with the Hatut Zeraze, Achebe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:07.600
Prince Namor, and other threats could reveal a&nbsp;
heretofore-unseen killer instinct in Ramonda.

